  "method": "Original deterministic integer pixel geometry in Java, without bitmap inputs. Use the existing hatch palette and arrow convention for ports. Metal gas cylinders have rounded shoulders, shaded walls, a top valve and gas/tier bands. No Minecraft, upstream, LibVulpes or third-party bitmap is copied, traced, sampled or transformed. Vanilla clients are read only for screening and external before/after evidence.",
  "planned_scope": [
    "Rolling-machine roller-and-sheet front and plain panelled sides for both v1.2 machines and all seven ports.",
    "Four dark framed port panels: item input/output arrows, fluid droplet and energy bolt.",
    "Three canister icons and four pressure-tier cylinder icons, with separate new texture names so earlier art and its reviews remain immutable.",
    "Texture-only model bindings in v1.8; no model shape, ID, behaviour, recipe, loot, historical resource, baseline casing or approved review changes."
  ],
